# Vibe Coder Quality Rules

## Error Resilience Defaults
- For external API calls, include timeout handling, structured error handling, and fallback behavior by default.
- Add bounded retry logic only for retry-safe operations.
- Log failures with contextual inputs (sanitized), not vague strings.

## Testability Requirements
- Prefer pure functions for core logic where possible.
- Use dependency injection or explicit interfaces around side effects (network, filesystem, DB, clock).
- Add fast "vibe-check" coverage for new behavior: happy path plus at least one failure or edge path.

## Security and Performance Checks
- Validate and sanitize untrusted input at boundaries.
- Avoid dynamic query/string construction when safe parameterization is available.
- Flag likely bottlenecks introduced by loops, repeated I/O, or N+1 patterns and remediate before handoff.

## Type and Interface Integrity
- Preserve strict typing and avoid unsafe type escapes.
- If API response/contract shape changes, update the corresponding type/interface in the same change.
- Handle caught errors defensively and narrow unknown values before use.
